## How to use this brain

**As an agent reading this:**
1. Read this index at session start.
2. If a project is active, read its file in `projects/`.
3. Write discoveries to `journal/YYYY-MM-DD.md` (append, don't overwrite). Hourly poker reflections stay here — do not put them in Recent Journal.
4. If something from journal has been referenced twice or more, promote it to `skills/` or `wiki/`.
5. When you choose a path over a real alternative, append to `decisions/log.md`. When something breaks or gets caught in review, append to `mistakes/log.md`. Check those before re-deciding or repeating work.
6. Keep this index in sync — update the tables above when files are added or status changes. After a batch of writes, run `brain lint`.
7. Update the Idea Bank ([wiki/ideabank.md](wiki/ideabank.md)) with every new project/product idea we generate.
8. Update the Shipped Builds Database ([wiki/portfolio-builds.md](wiki/portfolio-builds.md)) with every shipped build.
9. Grok: `~/.grok/rules/second-brain.md` is always on. Do not use `~/.grok/memory/` as a second vault.



**Directories:**
- `raw/` — unprocessed source material (paste links, dump notes, drop files here)
- `decisions/` — ledger of choices + tradeoffs (why, not just what)
- `mistakes/` — ledger of failures + how to avoid repeating them
- `wiki/` — compiled concept articles with [[backlinks]]
- `projects/` — live state per project
- `skills/` — reusable recipes and patterns that have earned their place
- `journal/` — dated discovery log; the cheap write layer
- `models/` — evidence-first model routing rules and evaluations
- `scripts/brain` — CLI source (`status|search|journal|recent|lint`)

